Mr. S, an advocate, is in the business of providing professional services like filing of petitions before Tribunals and Courts. Mrs. B, wife of Mr. S, is a registered Insolvency Professional (IP) with the IBBI. Mr. S, in his capacity of an advocate, filed many applications relating to admission of corporate debtors before NCLT and his wife Mrs. B being an insolvency professional in her own professional capacity acts as Insolvency Professional in all the cases her husband takes up. …";}s:8:"internal";a:2:{s:5:"cache";b:1;s:3:"toc";b:1;}s:8:"relation";a:1:{s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}s:11:"contributor";a:1:{s:5:"admin";s:11:"Atul Grover";}}s:10:"persistent";a:5:{s:4:"date";a:2:{s:7:"created";i:1760513401;s:8:"modified";i:1760513770;}s:7:"creator";s:11:"Atul Grover";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:11:"last_change";a:9:{s:4:"date";i:1760513770;s:2:"ip";s:11:"49.43.111.9";s:4:"type";s:1:"E";s:2:"id";s:18:"case_studies:case1";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:3:"sum";s:0:"";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:-11;s:4:"mode";s:4:"page";}s:11:"contributor";a:1:{s:5:"admin";s:11:"Atul Grover";}}}